## Test Quality Checklist

### Before Writing Tests
- [ ] Understand what behavior needs to be tested
- [ ] Identify edge cases and error conditions
- [ ] Plan test data and fixtures
- [ ] Consider test isolation and independence

### While Writing Tests
- [ ] Use descriptive test names
- [ ] Follow Arrange-Act-Assert pattern
- [ ] Write meaningful assertions
- [ ] Test both success and failure cases
- [ ] Keep tests focused and single-purpose

### After Writing Tests
- [ ] Verify tests pass consistently
- [ ] Check test coverage
- [ ] Review test readability
- [ ] Ensure tests are maintainable
- [ ] Document complex test scenarios

## Enforcement
Test quality standards are **MANDATORY** for all tests. Poor quality tests are worse than no tests. All tests must meet these standards before being merged into the codebase.
